      <div type="clause" n="El. 49.5">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> El. 49.5</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.5" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="44" ed="#liebermann"/>Þæm<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.11"/> halgan Gaste<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.12"/> wæs geðuht ⁊ ús, þæt we nane byrðenne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.13"/> on eow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.8"/> settan noldon ofer þæt ðe eow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.8"/> nedðearf wæs to healdanne: þæt [is<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.14"/>] ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi>, þæt ge forberen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.15"/>, þæt ge deofolgeld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.16"/> ne weorðien<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.17"/>, ne blod ne ðicggen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.18"/> ne asmorod, ⁊ from<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.19"/> diernum geligerum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.20"/>; ⁊ þæt ge willen, þæt oðre men eow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.8"/> ne don, ne doð ge ðæt oþrum monnum.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.5" corresp="#wit-g-prol-only"><pb n="44" ed="#liebermann"/>Þam halgam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.2"/> Gaste wæs geðuht ⁊ us, ðæt we nane byrþene on eow settan noldan ofer þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ðeow<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.2"/> niedþearf is to healdenne: þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> is ðonne, ðæt ge forberan, ðæt ge deofolgyld ne weorðian, ne blod ne ðicgan ne asmorod, ⁊ fra<hi rend="italic">m</hi> dyrnu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> geligeru<hi rend="italic">m</hi>; ⁊ þ<hi rend="italic">æt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.3"/></hi> ge willen, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> oðre men eow ne don, ne doþ ge ðæt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.4"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.5" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="45" ed="#liebermann"/>Ðæm halgan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.10"/> Gaste wæs geþuht ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.1"/> us, ðæt we nane byrþene<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.11-2"/> on eow setton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.1"/> noldon ofer ðæt ðe eow nydðearf wæs to healdene:<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.12-2"/> ðæt is þonne, ðæt ge forberan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.13-2"/>, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ge diofolgyld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.14-2"/> ne wurðian<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.15-2"/>, ne blod ne ðicgan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.13-2"/> ne asmorod, ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.1"/> from<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.1"/> dyrnum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.8-2"/> geligerum; ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.1"/> ðæt ge willan, ðæt oþre men eow ne don, ne do<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.16-2"/> ge ðæt oðrum monnum.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="El. 49.5" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="45" ed="#liebermann"/>Uisum est enim Spiritui sancto et nobis, nichil ultra imponere uobis oneris quam hęc necessario: ut abstineatis uos ab immolatis simulacrorum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.5"/> et sanguine et suffocato et fornicatione. A quibus custodientes uos, bene agetis. Valete.’<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.6"/> Quod uobis non uultis fieri, non faciatis alii.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.oe.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="MP 49.5" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="268" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Þæm halgan Gaste wæs geðuht ⁊ ús, þæt we nane byrðenne on eow settan noldon ofer þæt ðe eow nedðearf wæs to healdanne: þæt [is] ðon<hi rend="italic">ne</hi>, þæt ge forberen, þæt ge deofolgeld ne weorðien, ne blod ne ðicggen ne asmorod, ⁊ from diernum geligerum; ⁊ þæt ge willen, þæt oðre men eów ne don, ne doð ge ðæt oþrum monnum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="45" ed="#liebermann"/>Dem Heiligen Geiste und uns dünkte [richtig], dass wir keine Bürde auf euch legen wollten, über das hinaus, was zu halten euch nothwendig wäre: das heisst nämlich, dass ihr abstehet, Götzen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.de.1"/> anzubeten, Blut zu geniessen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.de.2"/> oder Ersticktes, und von unehelichen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.de.3"/> Buhlereien. Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_El-to-49-5.lnote.de.4"/> was ihr wollet, dass andere Leute euch nicht thun, thuet ihr das auch anderen Leuten nicht.’</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">It seemed [right] to the Holy Spirit and to us that we should lay no burden upon you beyond what it would be necessary for you to keep: that is to say, that you refrain from worshipping idols, from consuming blood or what is strangled, and from fornication outside marriage. And what you wish other people not to do to you, do not do that to other people either.’</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="269" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>It seemed to the Holy Ghost and to us, that we did not wish to impose on you any burden beyond what was needful to hold: that is, then, that you abandon the worship of devils, that you taste neither blood nor strangled [animals], and [that you keep] from [engagement in] fornication; and what you wish that other men not do to you, do not to other men.”</ab>
        <note type="passageSource">Acts 15,28–29; Matthew 7,12</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="45">A Apost. 15.28; A Apost. 15.29; Mat. 7.12</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">[15, 28] | [15, 29] | [Mat. 7, 12]</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="269"><label>see (same phrase diernum geligerum)</label> <ref target="clause:Af_El-to-6">Af El 6</ref> <quote>On diernum geligerum and its ambiguities, see MP §6 and n.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="269"><label>cf. (Golden Rule)</label> <ref target="clause:Grith_12">Grið 12</ref> <quote>Inexact renderings of this saying occur as well in Ælfric's explication ... and in the work of Wulfstan ...; cf. also Grið §12.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="383"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Iudex_Iudex-1">Iudex</ref> <quote>cf. Af Int. 40 – 46, 49:5–6, I Ew Pr., 2 – 2:1, II Ew 1:2 – 2, 8; II As 3:2, 25 – 25:1, V As 1:2–5, VI As 11</quote></note>
